Specification only (GPL-2.0, read, never copied): the piano MCA property protocol, its property ids and the stock policy values,
from Project-SunUEFI patches/linux/7.3/0001-platform.patch (drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c, GPL-2.0-only) and its
docs/devel/linux/kernel.md; Ubuntu's piano-charging.service (xiaomipad-8pro-mainline packaging) and the shipped xiaomi_mca.ko module
descriptions. PianoMca.c describes and implements that behaviour in its own code. The bq27z561 standard commands come from TI's
datasheet; the SM8750 addresses from piano's live DT (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb). Not used at all: the K90 annibale drivers
(APSL-2.0), Linux's qcom_battmgr, pmic_glink, qcom_q6v5_pas, bq27xxx and spmi-pmic-arb sources.
